# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DS AI Sales Agent — Phase 1
#
# Copy to `.env` and adjust. Phase 1 needs NO external API keys.
# Instagram passwords are never stored here — see `pnpm session:add`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# SQLite file. Path is relative to the project root.
DATABASE_URL="file:./prisma/dev.db"

# ── SAFETY ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1 = run the full pipeline (detect, classify, plan) but SEND NOTHING and mark
#     nothing READY. Use this for the first week to audit exactly what would
#     have gone out. This is the default; you must consciously turn it off.
DRY_RUN=1

# Comma-separated IST slot times the worker fires at.
SLOTS="11:00,15:00,17:00,20:00"
TZ="Asia/Kolkata"

# If a slot was missed while the machine was off, run it on boot when the miss
# is younger than this many minutes. Prevents silent skips without replaying
# stale slots from days ago.
CATCHUP_WINDOW_MINUTES=240

# ── OUTREACH GOVERNOR ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults; overridable per-pair in the DB.
DEFAULT_COOLDOWN_DAYS=7
# The ONE volume rule (2026-08-18, Tabish): messages one account may deliver to one
# recipient per IST day. Everything else is uncapped by his instruction.
MAX_PER_PAIR_PER_DAY=5
# Only use a detected campaign as a hook if it is fresher than this.
HOOK_MAX_AGE_HOURS=72

# ── SENDING (autopilot) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Human-like delay bounds between consecutive DMs, in seconds.
SEND_JITTER_MIN_SECONDS=45
SEND_JITTER_MAX_SECONDS=180
# Set true only after you have watched manual mode behave. Per-sender override
# lives on SenderAccount.autoSendEnabled — this is a global kill switch.
AUTOPILOT_ENABLED=false

# ── DASHBOARD ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fallback name recorded by the CLI ONLY, as "cli:<name>".
#
# The dashboard no longer uses this: it records the SIGNED-IN USER's email, because
# registration is open and one shared string would make the audit trail on three
# revenue accounts say the same thing no matter who pressed the button. The CLI has no
# session to read, so it keeps this — prefixed, so "pressed Send on the dashboard" and
# "typed y in a terminal" stay distinguishable in `sentBy`.
OPERATOR_NAME="Tabish"

# Set to 1 ONLY when the dashboard is served over HTTPS (a tunnel, or a hosted
# deployment). It marks the session cookie `secure`, and a secure cookie is not sent
# over plain HTTP — so setting it while running on http://127.0.0.1:3000 makes sign-in
# appear to succeed and then silently not work.
COOKIE_SECURE=0

# ── WHICH BROWSER `pnpm send` OPENS ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Must be the browser you are logged into the sending accounts in. Leave empty to
# use the macOS default https handler — but note the default is often Safari even
# when your Instagram session lives in Chrome, and the symptom is a login wall
# that looks like the agent lost your session. It never had one: the agent stores
# no Instagram credentials at all.
#
#   SEND_BROWSER="Google Chrome"   SEND_BROWSER="Brave Browser"   SEND_BROWSER="Safari"
SEND_BROWSER=""

# ── THE SCHEDULER ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The dashboard runs the watch in its own process, so starting the app is enough
# for slots to fire. Set false only when you run `pnpm worker` separately (a
# server). Whichever starts second sees the other's heartbeat and declines.
EMBEDDED_SCHEDULER=true

# ── READING THE TEXT IN A POST'S VIDEO ───────────────────────────────────────
# NOTHING TO CONFIGURE, AND NO API KEY. A paid placement can live entirely in the
# footage (the Thane bus, CLAUDE.md "THE CAPTION IS NOT THE POST"), and the
# decisive evidence there was TEXT on screen. That is read locally by Apple's
# Vision framework - offline, ~0.2s a frame, no network, no cost. Frames are
# saved to ~/.ds-sales-agent/frames. On Windows, install tesseract for a
# (measurably worse) fallback; without either, the dashboard SAYS frames are not
# being read rather than reporting clean footage.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ADDED 2026-08-17, AFTER CLONING THIS REPO THE WAY A SECOND OPERATOR WILL
#
# Everything below was read by the code and absent from this file. The first one
# is a DEAD END rather than an inconvenience, and nothing on screen says why.
# `tests/env-example.test.ts` now asserts this file covers every key the schema
# in `src/lib/env.ts` governs, so it cannot drift again.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── YOU CANNOT CREATE AN ACCOUNT WITHOUT THIS ────────────────────────────────
# An UNSET or empty code means signup is CLOSED. That is deliberate and correct on
# a server — a deployment without an invite code must refuse new accounts rather
# than offer an open door onto a page with a Send button — but on a fresh install it
# means you start the app, open /sign-up, and can never get in.
#
# Set it to any string you choose. The FIRST account created bootstraps as
# `operator`; everyone after is a `viewer` until an operator promotes them.
SIGNUP_INVITE_CODE="change-me-any-string"

# ── MAY THIS MACHINE DRIVE A BROWSER AND SEND? ───────────────────────────────
# DEFAULTS TO TRUE, and that is right for an operator's own Mac and wrong for a
# server. It is checked inside `withSendLock`, which every path that drives a
# browser passes through — the dispatcher, the dashboard's Send button, the
# on-demand dialog and the CLI.
#
# The hosted deployment sets this FALSE and must keep it false: a send drives a
# Chrome profile logged in BY HAND from a home IP, and copying that profile to a
# datacenter is a cookie transplant that works right up until enforcement lands.
#
# Set false while you are still reading what the agent would do.
SEND_ENABLED=true

# ── THE macOS INSTALLER, FOR THE DOWNLOAD BUTTON ─────────────────────────────
# Where the built .dmg lives so the hosted dashboard can serve it at
# /api/download/agent. The Linode cannot build a .dmg, so it is built on a Mac
# (bash scripts/build-dmg.sh) and the deploy copies it here. Unset falls back to
# <data-dir>/DS-Sales-Agent.dmg, which is where deploy.sh uploads it — so you
# rarely need to set this. A missing file just makes the button say "not published".
# AGENT_DMG_PATH=/root/.ds-sales-agent-data/DS-Sales-Agent.dmg

# ── THE LIFETIME CEILING ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Total messages ever put IN FLIGHT (SENT + REPLIED + SENDING + READY + QUEUED —
# not just delivered, or the planner would draft every pair before the ceiling
# bound). "unlimited" removes it. Start small on a new machine: this is the single
# cheapest brake while you are learning what it drafts.
MAX_TOTAL_SENDS=1

# ── CLASSIFYING POSTS THAT DO NOT DISCLOSE ───────────────────────────────────
# Without this key the classifier returns NO VERDICT — posts are still stored and
# still visible, and they stay UNCLASSIFIED, which means "not judged" and has never
# meant "ordinary". Detection of @madovermarketing_mom (a #Collaboration rule) works
# without it; @viralbhayani does not.
#
# Cost is negligible — measured at roughly two cents a day, with a 93%+ prompt cache
# hit. Get a key at platform.deepseek.com.
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=""

# ── THIS DEVICE'S NAME ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Labels this machine on the scheduler heartbeat and on device presence, so a shared
# database can say WHICH Mac last saw an account. Any short string.
DS_DEVICE_NAME="my-mac"

# ── DETECTION WINDOW (rarely changed) ────────────────────────────────────────
# ISO date. Posts older than this are stored but never sent to the classifier and
# never counted as "something new to say". Defaults to 2026-08-01 in code.
# DETECTION_CUTOFF="2026-08-01"

# ── OCR ON LINUX ONLY ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# macOS uses Apple's Vision framework and needs NOTHING here. A Linux host needs
# RapidOCR; this points at the python that has it.
# RAPIDOCR_PYTHON="/opt/ds-ocr-venv/bin/python"

# ── DEVELOPMENT ONLY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Count queries per page so `pnpm ig:layout` can assert a budget. The check FAILS
# rather than skips when this is off, so set it when running that command.
# DS_QUERY_COUNT=1
